  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the sources satisfy `requirements.ci.span`. The code implements each clause, and the tests cover the main points of the design space. I did not run the tests; this rests on reading the code and test bodies.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `colon_fence` in `src/lib.rs` accepts a line only if it has at most 3 leading spaces and at least three colons. It returns the colon count and the text after the colons.\n- `definition_blocks` in `src/lib.rs` requires the text after the colons to start with `{req}` (or `{example}` / `{definition}`). The prefix is matched with `strip_prefix`, so nothing may sit between the colons and `{req}`. It then requires whitespace and a valid name.\n- The closing fence is the first later line that meets three conditions:\n  - it is a colon fence,\n  - its colon count is at least the opening fence's count,\n  - nothing follows the colons.\n- That line must also lie outside Markdown code blocks. Code blocks are located with pulldown-cmark, so a `:::` inside a code block does not close the requirement.\n- The body is `body_start..body_end`: everything between the two fence lines, including headings, diagrams and blank lines. Text after the closing fence is excluded because `end` and `body_end` stop at the closing line.\n- `collect_definitions` in `src/evidence.rs` takes `content[body_start..body_end].trim()`, which excludes leading and trailing whitespace as required. It reports an unclosed fence as an error.\n- `replace_definitions` in `src/lib.rs` renders only closed blocks, using the same block boundaries.\n\n**Tests**\n- `colon_requirement_span_includes_markdown_and_excludes_following_text` in `src/evidence.rs` covers these cases:\n  - a body containing a fenced code block that holds `:::`, an ATX heading, a Setext heading and blank lines, all required to match evidence exactly;\n  - text after the closing fence, which is excluded;\n  - a second requirement following the first.\n- `reports_a_missing_closing_colon_fence` in `src/evidence.rs` covers the missing-closing-fence error.\n- `a_longer_colon_fence_contains_a_shorter_nested_directive` in `src/lib.rs` covers fence lengths. A `::::` opening is not closed by a nested `:::`. The body is the exact slice, and the text after the closing fence is outside the block.\n\n**Gaps**\n- I found no dedicated test for a malformed opening such as `:::` followed by a space before `{req}`. This is minor and arguably belongs to the identifiers requirement.\n- No FIXME comments or acknowledged gaps appear in the inputs.",
